    {
      "title": "Perceptron and Layers: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Perceptron and Layers: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Perceptron",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "output = ==activation(w·x + b)==",
                "**Weights** scale inputs; **bias** shifts the decision threshold",
                "One perceptron = ==one linear boundary==",
                "{red:XOR} is not linearly separable, so it fails"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Inputs x",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "w·x + b",
                    "sub": "weighted sum",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Activation",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Output",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dense Layer",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Many neurons, same input: ==y = f(W x + b)==",
                "W is shaped ==(out, in)==",
                "Params = ==in × out + out== (weights + biases)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "layer = nn.Linear(4, 3)  # W: (3, 4), b: (3,)",
                "sum(p.numel() for p in layer.parameters())  # 4*3 + 3 = 15"
              ],
              "note": "call-site fragment"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Why Stacking Needs Nonlinearity",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Linear layers only: W2(W1 x) = ==one linear map==",
                "Each layer needs a **nonlinear** activation",
                "Nonlinearity is what lets a stack solve XOR"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Depth needs activations",
              "text": "Without activations, N linear layers collapse into **one** linear layer."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why can one perceptron not solve XOR?** It draws only one linear boundary.",
                "**Params in Linear(784, 128)?** 784 × 128 + 128 = 100,480",
                "**Why do N linear layers collapse?** A product of matrices is a single matrix."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Activations: ReLU, Sigmoid, Softmax",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Activations: ReLU, Sigmoid, Softmax",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The three activations",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ReLU",
                "Sigmoid",
                "Softmax"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Formula",
                  "`max(0, x)`",
                  "`1/(1+e^-x)`",
                  "`e^xi / Σ e^xj`"
                ],
                [
                  "Output",
                  "0 to ∞",
                  "(0, 1)",
                  "probabilities, sum to 1"
                ],
                [
                  "Use",
                  "{green:hidden layers} (cheap default)",
                  "binary output",
                  "multi-class output"
                ],
                [
                  "Catch",
                  "{red:dying ReLU}: negative input, zero gradient",
                  "saturates, gradients vanish",
                  "overflow without max shift"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Match output to task",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Output",
                "Loss"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Binary",
                  "sigmoid",
                  "binary cross-entropy"
                ],
                [
                  "Multi-class",
                  "softmax",
                  "categorical cross-entropy"
                ],
                [
                  "Regression",
                  "none (linear)",
                  "MSE"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Stable softmax",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Subtract ==max(x)== before `exp`",
                "Result is unchanged, `exp` never overflows"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import math",
                "def softmax(xs):",
                "    m = max(xs)",
                "    e = [math.exp(x - m) for x in xs]",
                "    return [v / sum(e) for v in e]"
              ],
              "note": "definition only, call it with your logits"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Hidden layers: ==ReLU==. Output layer: sigmoid, softmax or nothing, chosen by the task."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Forward Pass and Backpropagation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Forward Pass and Backpropagation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Forward Pass",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Feed input ==layer by layer==: `a = f(W a_prev + b)`",
                "{blue:Cache} each layer's input `a_prev` and pre-activation `z`",
                "Backward pass reuses the cache instead of recomputing"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Backpropagation",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Chain rule== from loss to each weight: `dL/dW = dL/da · da/dz · dz/dW`",
                "{red:Vanishing gradients}: repeated factors below 1 shrink the signal",
                "Sigmoid derivative peaks at ==0.25==; **ReLU** (slope 1 for x > 0) eases it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Quantity",
                "Formula"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Weight gradient",
                  "`dW = δ · a_prevᵀ`"
                ],
                [
                  "Bias gradient",
                  "`db = δ`"
                ],
                [
                  "Error passed back",
                  "`δ_prev = Wᵀ δ ⊙ f'(z)`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Training Step",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Forward",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Loss",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Zero grads",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backward",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Step",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "pred = model(x)",
                "loss = loss_fn(pred, y)",
                "optimizer.zero_grad()",
                "loss.backward()",
                "optimizer.step()"
              ],
              "note": "call-site fragment; model, x, y defined elsewhere"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Zero the gradients",
              "text": "PyTorch ==accumulates== gradients across batches. Skip `zero_grad()` and each step uses a **sum** of old and new gradients."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why cache z?** Backward needs `f'(z)` and `a_prev`.",
                "**Why does sigmoid vanish?** Derivative is at most 0.25, so deep products shrink."
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
