              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Epochs, Batches, Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Epoch== = one full pass over the training set",
                "==Iteration== = one batch update",
                "Iterations per epoch = `N / batch_size`",
                "==Shuffle== training data every epoch",
                "{red:Never} shuffle or augment the validation set"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Batch size",
                "Behaviour"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Full batch",
                  "stable, slow, memory heavy"
                ],
                [
                  "Mini-batch",
                  "the usual compromise"
                ],
                [
                  "Size 1",
                  "noisy updates"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dropout and Early Stopping",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Training",
                    "sub": "zero fraction p, scale 1/(1−p)",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "model.eval()",
                    "sub": "dropout off",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dropout is a ==regularizer==",
                "Typical `p`: ==0.2–0.5== for dense layers",
                "==Early stopping==: val loss rises while train loss falls"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "model.train()  # dropout on",
                "...",
                "model.eval()  # dropout off",
                "with torch.no_grad():",
                "    preds = model(x_val)"
              ],
              "note": "call-site fragment"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot eval()?",
              "text": "Dropout stays on at inference, so predictions are ==noisy==."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why shuffle each epoch?** Stops order-dependent learning; gradients are less correlated, more representative.",
                "**Why rescale by 1/(1−p)?** Keeps expected activation equal in training and eval."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
